# DURABLE REPRO — the SPAWN argument face never reads `arg.node.ownership`, so
# `spawn f(&c.fd)` silently drops the callee's write.
#
# THE MECHANISM. `spawn.rs` lowers spawn arguments with a bare
# `lower_expr(ctx, builder, &arg.node.value)` at three sites and never consults
# `arg.node.ownership`, bypassing `lower_call_arg` and BOTH `&`-formation faces
# entirely. The sigil is simply not there by the time the argument is lowered.
#
# 🚨 THE DIVERGENCE IS NEW, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF COMMITTING THIS NOW.
# Measured, both `gg check`-clean, on the same program:
#
#   | spelling             | before Family-1 | after Family-1 |
#   |----------------------|-----------------|----------------|
#   | `bumpi(&c.fd)`       | 10 (wrong)      | **110** (fixed) |
#   | `spawn bumpi(&c.fd)` | 10 (wrong)      | **10** (still wrong) |
#
# So two spellings of one intent were EQUALLY WRONG and are now SILENTLY
# DIVERGENT. That is strictly more dangerous than the old state: a reader who
# verifies the direct call now has every reason to believe the spawned one works.
#
# ⚠ THIS FACE IS TYPE-INDEPENDENT, unlike Family-1's. Measured on the same shape:
# `spawn bumpv(&c.vd)` (`Vector[int]`) also loses its `push` — and `Vector` is
# one of the four types that worked BY ACCIDENT at the call-arg face. So the
# spawn face is NOT the projected-TYPE axis; do not file it as another Family-1
# cell. (`spawn bumps(&c.sd)` on a `String` field fails the C build outright — a
# third symptom of the same face, already filed separately.)
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): 110 / 110 — the spawned call's write-through reaches
# the caller exactly as the direct call's does.
#
# NOT Family-1's to fix: the fix must teach the spawn arg lowering to honour
# `arg.node.ownership`, ideally by routing those three sites through
# `lower_call_arg` so they inherit both `&`-formation faces at once (Core #4 —
# fix the class at the producer, not the instance). Cited from TODO.md's
# consumption-limb census entry, which already names the three sites.
#
# Seeds are computed, never literals.
struct C:
    int fd

int seed():
    return 10

void bumpi(int &n):
    n = n + 100

void main():
    C c = C(seed())
    bumpi(&c.fd)
    print(c.fd)

    C c2 = C(seed())
    spawn bumpi(&c2.fd)
    print(c2.fd)
